      "text": "The given equation means the following, where $c = f(x)$,\n\\[ g(c) = 3x + 4.\\] Implication implies immediately that $c = 2x - 5$.\nSo now we have that $f(x) = \\boxed{11}$ for all $x$.\nAlternatively, we can replace $x$ by any number.  For example, if we let $x = 3$, then $f(3) = 3a + b$ and $g(f(3))=3(3a+b) - 5=9a + 3b -5=3(3 a+b)-(-5) = 9a + 3 b + 15$, which must be equal to $9a + 3b + 4$.  Thus, $11 = -1$ which implies $a+b=10$. The answer is 10",
